# The login program's sign-in with a PIN (docs/adr/0020-oxy-account-login.mdx, decision 2): an
# enrolled Oxy account's PIN, checked by oxyos-accountd against its verifier, offline, and
# throttled there (oxyos-pin-check), the account checked, and the person's session opened as
# oxyos-login opens one. Never the password, and never online. Installed as
# /etc/pam.d/oxyos-login-pin.
# pam_exec's refusal is a system error to PAM: a wrong PIN is turned into an ordinary rejection
# (pam_deny), which the throttles count, and an accepted one establishes credentials (pam_permit),
# as common-auth's pam_unix lines do.
auth [success=1 default=ignore] pam_exec.so quiet expose_authtok /usr/libexec/oxyos/oxyos-pin-check
auth requisite pam_deny.so
auth required pam_permit.so
@include common-account
session required pam_loginuid.so
session optional pam_keyinit.so force revoke
session required pam_limits.so
session required pam_env.so readenv=1
session required pam_env.so readenv=1 envfile=/etc/default/locale
session required pam_unix.so
session required pam_systemd.so
